17592186045417] [17592186501080 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501080 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186500868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501080 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "899ae17d-d211-5d95-aea6-b05439a6e74e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501090 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501090 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500704 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501090 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501090 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501090 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501090 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501090 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501090 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186500675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501090 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a16204f8-f3d9-5011-8c48-c6b5f2db3a5b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501091 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500534 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501091 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501091 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501091 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501091 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500945 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501091 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501091 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501091 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186500534 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501091 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a301872e-f9c1-5a36-8e8e-3c31baa4c791" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501153 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501091 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501153 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110484" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501153 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501153 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501153 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "294d3a87-ec82-5ba0-946d-47e92c2e2260" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501153 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501159 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501159 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75111" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501159 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501159 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501159 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3bf6c999-4f9a-599b-886e-437d5517ddbb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501159 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501170 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501090 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501170 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110472" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501170 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501170 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501170 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "62e49a58-91d5-5a4c-a1e9-c098f0c19c7c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501170 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501214 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501214 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110493" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501214 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501214 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:=3{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501214 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b525e6cc-0aa9-5691-bec6-c50f5a129f63" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501214 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{2}:=3{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operation is ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501239 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501239 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75161" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501239 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501239 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:=\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501239 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f10c9aaf-98e6-52a7-9de1-c8d29489c892" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501239 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501249 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "12f00de3-338f-56d2-8859-359b23733d90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501249 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186501214 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501251 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186501273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501251 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "178fbde8-4f97-53f7-bac7-f88af87a8d55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501251 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186501239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501260 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186501249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592